    <!--
        2026-08-31, THIRD wire-fraud code-review pass — Blocked_By__c, Transaction_Deal__c,
        Task_Group__c and Task_Sequence__c FLIPPED editable=true -> false (both Event.* and Task.*).
        Three rounds of review found four distinct bypasses of Prerequisite_Must_Be_Met_To_Complete,
        all the same family: the gate's state (Blocked_By__c) lives on the record it protects, and
        every working persona held editable=true on the fields that let it be repointed or defeated -
        blank the key; repoint the key to something already complete; repoint Transaction_Deal__c to
        a different deal whose prerequisite is already Completed (one DML statement, no Apex
        involved); or renumber the PREREQUISITE's own Task_Sequence__c so the key stops resolving,
        clear it, then complete. Every one of those needs an editable=true grant on ordinary
        Task-Edit FLS - this closes the UI, list-view inline edit, Data Loader and REST-as-user paths
        for all four in one change.
        DOES NOT STOP: system-mode Apex or a system-context Flow (FLS is not evaluated there) - the
        developer agent is adding a code-level deal-scope check as defence in depth for that gap.
        VERIFIED BEFORE FLIPPING (per code review's explicit checklist): grepped every consumer of
        Blocked_By__c / Transaction_Deal__c / Task_Group__c / Task_Sequence__c across
        force-app/main/default/{classes,lwc,flows,flexipages} - every writer is Apex
        (TaskFanoutService.fanOutNow, which writes `Database.insert(toInsert, true,
        AccessLevel.SYSTEM_MODE)` - unaffected by FLS). ZERO LWCs (including transactionTaskGroups,
        transactionPhaseCards, transactionChecklistSummary) or Flows reference any of these four
        fields at all, so there is no `lightning-record-edit-form` silently dropping them on a
        success toast - the historical failure mode this repo has already paid for once. Confirmed by
        grep, not assumed.
        BREAKS scripts/backfill-task-blocked-by.apex, WHICH RUNS AS ANONYMOUS APEX AND THEREFORE
        ENFORCES THE RUNNING USER'S FLS. That is expected and intentional, not a regression to
        silently work around - see Transaction_Prereq_Override_Access.permissionset-meta.xml, the
        admin-only escape hatch created in the same pass, which the backfill runner (and the M5
        migration, and any Phase 1 repair of a resolvable-but-wrong key) must hold in addition to
        this set.
    -->
